//RS /// Lower an `if` and its else-if chain (an `else` that is exactly one `if`,
//RS /// which is how every N-arm decision table reaches TIR) in a loop rather than
//RS /// one recursion per arm. The loop holds borrowed links, so the walk is linear
//RS /// in the arm count. Blocks, scopes, shadow restores, and terminators are
//RS /// emitted in exactly the order the nested `lower_stmts` -> `lower_stmt` ->
//RS /// `lower_if` calls produced. The Jet compiler's `jet_codegen_lower_if` emits
//RS /// the same order by direct recursion, since a Jet local holding the rest of
//RS /// the chain would be a copy of it.
